<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!--

  The M3 type scale, wired into the theme's textAppearance* attributes. The layouts still set
  inline sp literals; they stop doing that as each screen is rebuilt, and from then on a layout
  should set android:textAppearance="?attr/textAppearanceX" rather than android:textSize.

  The oversized Metric.* styles for the Record readout and the large numerals are not here yet:
  nothing references them until those screens are rebuilt, so they land with them.

  ── TYPEFACE ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Bricolage Grotesque (SIL OFL), bundled in res/font/. It replaced the platform sans-serif.

  It ships as a VARIABLE font whose default instance is "96pt ExtraBold", so weight and optical size
  are stated explicitly in bricolage_display.xml and bricolage_text.xml. Omit them and the entire app
  renders extra-bold at an optical size drawn for billboards. Display and headline tiers take opsz
  40; everything from title down takes opsz 14, because the 96pt cut's tight spacing and fine details
  fall apart at the 11sp unit labels.

  Hard constraint for any candidate typeface: FULL VIETNAMESE COVERAGE. The app is named
  "Chạy Ngay Đi" and its copy is Vietnamese, so the family must render ạ ẹ ị ọ ụ ỵ đ ơ ư ề ế ộ ậ
  correctly - stacked diacritics, not just Latin Extended-A. Bricolage, Inter and Roboto all do.
  Many fashionable display faces do not; verify before committing.

  ── TABULAR FIGURES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Every style below sets fontFeatureSettings="tnum". Without it, proportional digits make the running
  timer visibly jitter as digits change width, and metric columns fail to align. This is the single
  highest-value typographic detail in a tracking app.

  It is now load-bearing rather than advisory. Roboto's digits were tabular by default, so this rule
  was documented for months and applied nowhere and nothing looked wrong. Bricolage's are not: its
  "1" is 310 units against its "0" at 608. Any future typeface must either carry tnum or have tabular
  digits by default - Be Vietnam Pro was rejected for having neither.
-->
<resources>

    <!-- ============================================================
         DISPLAY · editorial hero type. Negative tracking is what makes
         large type read as designed rather than merely big.
         ============================================================ -->
    <style name="TextAppearance.ChayNgayDi.DisplayLarge" parent="TextAppearance.Material3.DisplayLarge">
        <item name="android:fontFamily">@font/bricolage_display</item>
        <item name="fontFamily">@font/bricolage_display</item>
        <item name="android:fontFeatureSettings">tnum</item>
        <item name="android:textSize">57sp</item>
        <item name="lineHeight">64sp</item>
        <item name="android:letterSpacing">-0.025</item>
    </style>

    <style name="TextAppearance.ChayNgayDi.DisplayMedium" parent="TextAppearance.Material3.DisplayMedium">
        <item name="android:fontFamily">@font/bricolage_display</item>
